# Line endings: this project stores LF in the repository.
#
# Why this file exists: on Windows, editing a file with a tool that writes CRLF
# made 18 files show every line as changed, turning a 767-line diff into 9017
# lines of noise. That is not cosmetic -- it made the Round 83 refactor
# unreviewable until the endings were restored by hand.
#
# `text=auto` lets git normalise on commit, and `eol=lf` makes the working tree
# match the repository, so an editor that writes CRLF is corrected instead of
# committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary

# Windows-only helper scripts keep CRLF because cmd.exe and PowerShell expect it.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
